  <item>
    <title>Sasha / John Digweed – Northern Exposure</title>
    <link>https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/sasha-john-digweed-northern-exposure/</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="true">https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/sasha-john-digweed-northern-exposure/</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 04:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <enclosure url="https://media.pitchfork.com/photos/6ab6f1223e0766e51cb65f45/16:9/w_1280,c_limit/Sasha%20and%20Digweed%20-%20Northern%20Exposure%20album%20art.png" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/>
    <description><![CDATA[<p>Each Sunday, Pitchfork takes an in-depth look at a significant album from the past, and any record not in our archives is eligible. Today, we revisit the British DJs’ monumental 1996 mix, a virtuosic blend of after-hours grooves and floor-filling intensity that helped to canonize the elusive sound of progressive house.</p>
<img src="https://media.pitchfork.com/photos/6ab6f1223e0766e51cb65f45/16:9/w_1280,c_limit/Sasha%20and%20Digweed%20-%20Northern%20Exposure%20album%20art.png" alt="Northern Exposure cover"/>
